\"PKT-0016 client breakdown gave direct evidence that open and apply time sit in the client editor.\"},\"missing\":{\"ref\":\"atlas/sdkjs-word.md\",\"text\":\"Card oracle says none without checking external/sdkjs/tests/word; no graph.json or line metrics for external modules.\"},\"hindered\":{\"ref\":\"adapter#factory\",\"text\":\"Read-only pipelines (find -exec wc, chained ls/head) were refused by permissions.\"}}' >> .theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl\ngrep -q \"^verdict: \" .theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-sdkjs-word.md && grep -q \"^goals_hash: dcb03039\" .theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-sdkjs-word.md && echo ok; theseus validate 2>&1 | tail -5"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":22,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the diagnosis to `.theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-sdkjs-word.md` and committed it as `4932f9d`. The verdict is **refactor** (staying in JavaScript), with confidence low, and it only holds if a planned profiling packet confirms the time is in this module. All three acceptance commands pass; `theseus validate` reports 0 errors and 1 warning, which I did not look into.\n\n**Why refactor:** this module is where users wait.\n- **Opening:** after Editor.bin arrives, a docx takes 1.9–2.4 s to parse, lay out and render, and that grows with document size.\n- **Co-editing:** the slow cases (p90 105–143 ms) come from the receiving browser applying the change, not the server.\n- **Typing:** p90 is 119–156 ms on 10- and 100-page documents, above the ~50 ms point where people notice.\n\nWhat's missing is a split between this module, the shared sdkjs code, fonts and the browser.\n\n**Discarded:**\n- **Keep:** it would leave the largest client cost untouched.\n- **Migrate or rewrite:** no oracle is established yet (rule D1), the hotspot is unknown, and the model is tightly tied to sdkjs's shared globals. Moving it to Rust/WASM would mean copying data across the boundary on every edit.\n- **Retire:** this is the live document editor.\n\n**Packet plan (wave 0):**\n- **P1:** profile opening, typing and applying remote changes on the PKT-0016 sample documents, split by part of the module. It needs the running Document Server and a browser. Its result decides the actual refactor packets, or downgrades the verdict to keep.\n- **P2:** run the existing word test suites as the oracle and update the Atlas card.\n\n**Surprise:** the Atlas card says there is no oracle, but `external/sdkjs/tests/word/` has 21 QUnit test suites that already run headless in upstream CI.\n\n**Not done:**\n- Permissions refused the commands I tried for line counts, so I used the card's figure of about 428k lines.\n- I did not run the test suites; that is P2's job.\n- I did not read any other diagnosis of this module, to keep it independent.\n\nThe Executor log and the friction line are written.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- Cards for external modules should check for test suites in the sibling repository before setting the oracle level.\n- External modules have no `graph.json` or size metrics yet.","ttft_ms":1909,"type":"result","duration_ms":86975,"uuid":"5a759d26-175a-4b7d-b2f4-6bcc9321f28b","ttft_stream_ms":911,"time_to_request_ms":358,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":214,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":26,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":8,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":4,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":14,"model_gates":0,"too